# Patches are fed to `git apply` verbatim, by CMake, at configure time
# (tools/riven-convert/CMakeLists.txt). Git on Windows checks out with
# core.autocrlf=true by default, and a patch whose body has been translated to
# CRLF while its hunk headers still count LF bytes is rejected as "corrupt patch
# at <line>" -- which is exactly how the Windows converter build failed, at
# 0001-pack-mohawk-file-table.patch:29, before this file existed.
#
# -text means "never translate line endings on this path, in either direction".
*.patch -text
